{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/592342-can-you-communicate-with-the-dreaming","id":592342,"title":"Can you communicate with the Dreaming?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T22:42:49-07:00","id":592342,"title":"Can you communicate with the Dreaming?","content":"In the Umbra, I sometimes get the sense that space is almost an illusion and the place is built out of gafflings, jagglings, and gods of various power. The &quot;place&quot; you see around you is simply the spirits providing you with a medium by which you can interact with them. But not so with the Dreaming. Though the Dreaming surely has its share of powerful beings, the Dreaming by itself seems to be w living thing, and even seems to think for itself, after a fashion. <br /> <br /> Now, reading again how the Order of Hermes cuts deals even with Paradox spirits, and reading about how the Dreamspeakers will send general messages through out the Umbra, is there a way to bargain with the Dreaming, possibly through powerful intermediaries, so that you can get support at a later date or get it to grant Fae specific boons like knowledge of how to break the curse on House Liam or find a lost Treasure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T05:35:40-07:00","id":592540,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a good basis for a chronicle to me!<br /> <br /> It certainly wouldn't be easy. The heart of the Dreaming is Arcadia, and Arcadia is cut off completely from the rest of the Dreaming. Looking a prophecies, signs, and other subtle messages in dreams is probably the closest your average changeling gets to communicating directly with the Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T16:46:02-07:00","id":593282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/592342-can-you-communicate-with-the-dreaming#post592342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Umbra, I sometimes get the sense that space is almost an illusion and the place is built out of gafflings, jagglings, and gods of various power. The &quot;place&quot; you see around you is simply the spirits providing you with a medium by which you can interact with them. But not so with the Dreaming. Though the Dreaming surely has its share of powerful beings, the Dreaming by itself seems to be w living thing, and even seems to think for itself, after a fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming . . .alive? Hmm . . . interesting concept. I've always considered it as sort of a tangible manifestation of humanity's subconscious . . . or at least the part that dreams/creates/inspires. Communicating with it might well be tantamount to interacting with the &quot;hive mind&quot; of all humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, reading again how the Order of Hermes cuts deals even with Paradox spirits, and reading about how the Dreamspeakers will send general messages through out the Umbra, is there a way to bargain with the Dreaming, possibly through powerful intermediaries, so that you can get support at a later date or get it to grant Fae specific boons like knowledge of how to break the curse on House Liam or find a lost Treasure? </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that there <i>is</i> objective knowledge in the Dreaming. You're talking about a reality built of dreams, wishes, and hopes . . .does such a place even <i>have</i> rules or (meta)physical laws, the way we tend to think of them?<br /> <br /> Take the curse on House Liam - did it stick because the other sidhe used some obscure arcane knowledge? Or because such a curse makes for a great story, and thus became &quot;real&quot; within the Dreaming? Ultimately, curing it might not be a matter of spell books or spirit pacts - it might be a matter of going on some impossible quest that forms a <i>better</i> story. After all, doesn't everyone want their fairy tales to end with &quot;and they all lived happily ever after&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T18:14:22-07:00","id":593415,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I didn't mean House Liam, I meant House Leanhaune!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T03:24:25-07:00","id":594607,"title":"","content":"Yup. In theory all you need is Primal 1 and Fae 5. But it would be a lot like trying to power a single LED bulb with a Tesla coil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}